s, only one is returned.\"\n}"}],"structured_content":{"suggested":[{"slug":"2026-09-23-app-review-wants-test-credentials-but-my-app-only-had-google","title":"App review wants test credentials, but my app only had Google sign-in","stack":"OAuth 2.1 · AWS Lambda (Python) · app-directory submission (OpenAI Apps / Anthro","tier":"T0","capability":"T0 · inert — touches nothing","why":"matches app, oauth"},{"slug":"2026-04-15-intervals-icu-oauth-quirks-no-refresh-token-duplicate-scope-","title":"Intervals.icu OAuth quirks — no refresh_token, \"Duplicate scope\", and why the init endpoint must be POST","stack":null,"tier":"T0","capability":"T0 · inert — touches nothing","why":"matches intervals.icu, oauth"},{"slug":"2026-09-14-adding-google-sign-in-so-non-developers-can-use-your-app","title":"Adding Google sign-in so non-developers can use your app","stack":"Google OAuth 2.0 · Python/AWS Lambda backend · vanilla-JS SPA","tier":"T0","capability":"T0 · inert — touches nothing","why":"matches app, oauth"}],"about_tiers":"Tier is a CAPABILITY (blast-radius) disclosure, not a safety verdict: higher just means look closer. Run check_capability on the live files before applying a story.","note":"Read each with get_story, and run check_capability before applying. Fewer, closer matches beat a padded list — if only one story truly fits, only one is returned."}},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
